<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25733" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαρρήγνῡμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>break through,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά τε ῥήξασθαι ἐπάλξεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.308
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαρρήξασα χαλινόν</span>
			<i>having broken</i> the bridle <i>asunder,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				259
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγις ἂν . . διαρρήξειας [τὴν
				κεφαλήν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλευρὰν διαρρήξαντα . . φασγάνῳ</span>
			<i>having cloven</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				834
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὰς χορδάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					86a
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>burst,</i> as with eating, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.2.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxil.
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phoenicid.
				3
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μυρίων ἀγαθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					10D.
				</span></i>
			; with passion, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαρραγήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					340
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ φθόνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἂν σὺ διαρραγῇς ψευδόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.21
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαρραγείης,</span> as a curse,
				<i>'split you!'</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, etc.: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διέρρωγα</span>
			<i>to be broken</i> or <i>torn,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διερρωγυιῶν τῶν χορδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
				</span></i>
			 l. c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκεσαμένη τὸ διερρωγός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					623a18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόδημα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.82b
				</span></i>
			: later pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διερρηγμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.64c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
